KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ deduced pack arity through partial-spec base: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG must FAIL: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
A class template partial specialization whose parameter pack follows fixed
(non-deduced) template arguments, selected via the partial-specialization
disambiguation path (as a dependent base class), must deduce the pack to all
trailing arguments rather than collapsing it to one element.  This is the shape
of libstdc++'s __result_of_impl<false,false,_Functor,_ArgTypes...> behind
multi-argument std::function.  N5008 [temp.spec.partial.match], [temp.variadic]/5.

A targeted fix exists (expand the deduced pack into positional arguments in
disambiguate_template_classes, mirroring elaborate_class_template), and it makes
this test and the synthetic __invoke_result models pass.  It is NOT yet landed
because it unblocks multi-argument std::function construction far enough to hit
a separate, pre-existing blocker -- the std::function _Base_manager::_M_create /
_Function_handler::_M_manager member-function-template bodies are converted but
do not reach the goto model ("no body"), which also affects single-argument
std::function and currently makes cpp17_functional_basic pass only vacuously.
Land this fix together with that body-propagation fix.
